It’s best to include `[PexAssumeUnderTest]` attribute on the method parameters to avoid unnecessary test with default values. This will make the test more meaningful and reduce the total number of testing cases.

### 3. Use Assumptions, Observe and Customize Assertions.

Assertion is a crucial part to validate if the method under test behaves as expected. In the previous examples, we used `Debug.Assert` to let you quickly inspect your code during debugging. You can also customize the assertion based on your needs. 

For instance, in the PUT_IndexOfContract test method, we customized the assertion to validate if the return value is non-negative when your list contains the specified element. If the element does not exist in the list, the return value should be -1.

## Conclusion

Partial testing is an essential tool in automatic testing because it helps in catching and fixing bugs early. Pex (Pex/Stock) is a powerful tool that provides input generation for unit testing. In addition to random value generation, Pex also provides advanced features like constraint-based testing and method reactive testing. By integrating Pex into your test projects, you can benefit from rigorous testing approach to ensure the quality and reliability of your applications.

Remember, the effectiveness of Pex testing is highly dependent on the quality of your input parameters and the quality of the generated tests, so it always recommended to design your test cases with a focus on edge and boundary conditions. 

Happy testing, and stay tuned for the next blog post where we will discuss more about Pex testing in depth.

***References:***

- [Pex/Stock documentation](http://research.microsoft.com/en-us/um/cambridge/projects/pex/)
- [Introduction to Pex](https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2012/09/01-introducing-pex.aspx)
- [Pex Tips and Tricks](https://marcos.adadev.com/2011/08/13/pex-tips-and-tricks-1/)
- [Microsoft Research: Partial Testing with Pex](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=15480)
- [Pex for Everyone](https://stackify.com/pex-for-everyone/)

*(Note: the article is part of a series on testing methodology using Microsoft Fakes and Pex)*.
